WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:13.458
B-but...why are you leaving?

00:00:14.166 --> 00:00:15.666
I'm a free agent now

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:18.166
Will you be back?

00:00:19.291 --> 00:00:21.791
Yes, one way or another

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.750
Your Stashe Brother Steven will look after you now

00:00:25.041 --> 00:00:28.083
You will be in good hands...dlebars

00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.083
She'll be a'right

00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:31.833
Well, I must be going now

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:33.583
It's time for me to test the markets

00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:34.958
Ya! Ya!

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.666
Fare thee well, brothers!

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:37.541
Good on ya, mate!

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:49.083
Farewell Kevin

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:50.541
Now

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:52.416
I do what I want

00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:01.791
I know you and Russ had your issues,

00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:03.250
but I can assure you

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:06.041
there will be no such chemistry problems here

00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:07.500
Well that’s nice to hear

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.250
Plus you’ll have the services of the premier

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.875
point guard in the realm

00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:14.791
Wait, uh, so better than Steph Curry?

00:01:14.791 --> 00:01:17.041
Well, certainly top three

00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:20.125
Well, there’s Russell and Chris Paul...

00:01:20.125 --> 00:01:23.125
Top three point guard...in the East is what I meant

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.708
OK um, well then there’s Kyrie Irving--

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:27.541
Kyrie’s gotta be No. 1

00:01:27.541 --> 00:01:30.250
and then Kyle Lowry...he’s pretty good these days

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.250
And Isaiah Thomas? Honestly underrated--

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.041
Shut up Bradley!

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:33.291
Do you want him to play here or not!

00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.708
Well I’m just being honest!

00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:36.041
Oh you want honesty?

00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:37.916
I’d be top three EASY if my max contract 

00:01:37.916 --> 00:01:39.625
shooting guard wasn’t always INJURED

00:01:39.625 --> 00:01:41.208
Oh, so sorry John!

00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:42.500
I put my body on the line for this team!

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.791
(mocking, falsetto): Oh, I’m Bradley! I’m made of glass!

00:01:44.916 --> 00:01:47.291
Will you two twits shut up!

00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:49.166
(sigh)

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:52.166
As I was saying, uh, the chemistry here...

00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:54.333
definitely top five...

00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:55.250
in the East

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:08.125
So...uh, what’s that...

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:10.750
what’s that over there? What’s that box?

00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:12.708
Soul Box

00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:16.166
I’m sorry, you said “soul box”?

00:02:16.166 --> 00:02:17.791
Soul Box

00:02:18.125 --> 00:02:20.625
Soul box. So...like a box...

00:02:21.166 --> 00:02:22.583
for souls?

00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:25.000
When you sign with the Spurs

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:28.666
your soul and your personality are put into the box

00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:32.041
Riiiiight. So...

00:02:32.125 --> 00:02:34.500
do I get it back?

00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:37.000
Indubitably

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:40.541
Ha, ha, ha, ha, haaaa

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.083
So

00:02:44.666 --> 00:02:47.375
What are your thoughts on tankin'?

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.250
Oh it’s true

00:02:51.541 --> 00:02:54.666
If you were to join us, you’d be endlessly ridiculed,

00:02:54.666 --> 00:02:56.708
your old teammates will despise you 

00:02:56.708 --> 00:02:58.916
and the fans in Oklahoma will cook their stew 

00:02:58.916 --> 00:03:00.916
on the flames of your burning jersey

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:03.083
People will call you a traitor,

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.083
a coward

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:07.916
and some may say you’ve destroyed the entire balance of the realm

00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:11.041
But...on the other hand!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.916
If you were to join us, we would be...

00:03:17.375 --> 00:03:18.500
so good

00:03:21.291 --> 00:03:22.291
Cleveland!

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:24.625
This is for you!

00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:30.708
But we will win not just one championship!

00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:32.791
Not two!

00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:35.875
LeBron, um, sorry, uh...you might want to read this

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.375
Can this wait?

00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:38.250
Not three!

00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:40.750
It concerns some changes next year

00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:44.041
If this is about Delly going to the Bucks...I think we’ll live

00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:47.500
Not four but...!

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:53.458
Um...But one is fine!

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:56.000
Some people never get championships

00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:59.083
And we should be happy with this one

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.550
Well we’re all very excited to have you here

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.633
But I must warn you, the Garpax has eyes EVERYWHERE

00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:22.883
Be careful what you say

00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:24.591
and let your game do the talking

00:04:24.841 --> 00:04:25.758
Have no doubt,

00:04:25.758 --> 00:04:28.800
I’m as healthy as ever AND I shoot threes now

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.925
There’s no reason we can’t form a superteam

00:04:30.925 --> 00:04:33.050
Is that...is that Dwyane Wade?
—here in Chicago

00:04:33.466 --> 00:04:35.300
Oh Seven Hells 

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.633
It is. It is you!

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:38.633
Who is that?

00:04:38.675 --> 00:04:39.675
Someone you know?

00:04:39.675 --> 00:04:40.550
Mario Chalmers

00:04:40.591 --> 00:04:42.008
We used to play together in Miami

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.716
Oh great, here we go

00:04:45.091 --> 00:04:45.925
Hello Rio

00:04:46.508 --> 00:04:47.508
Nooooo

00:04:47.925 --> 00:04:49.925
You’re on the Bulls now?

00:04:50.383 --> 00:04:52.508
Oh that’s so WEIRD

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.841
We was on a superteam together

00:04:55.508 --> 00:04:56.508
“The Big Four!”

00:04:56.841 --> 00:04:58.258
‘Member those days, Dwyane?

00:04:58.466 --> 00:04:59.175
...no?

00:04:59.175 --> 00:05:00.925
But I can’t blame you for leaving really

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:02.300
Twilight-a your career...

00:05:02.341 --> 00:05:04.216
bad knees, bad shoulders...

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.133
maybe you can scrape together one last playoff run with...

00:05:07.591 --> 00:05:08.591
sorry what’s your name?

00:05:09.258 --> 00:05:10.258
Jimmy Butler

00:05:10.716 --> 00:05:11.716
Oh

00:05:12.008 --> 00:05:14.091
You DO look a lot like Michael Jordan

00:05:14.091 --> 00:05:16.175
Well it’s all very exciting

00:05:16.175 --> 00:05:17.883
We must be going now, I’m afraid

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.966
Oh. Alright, um, well,

00:05:20.008 --> 00:05:21.008
if you need a point guard

00:05:21.758 --> 00:05:22.716
or whatever...

00:05:22.716 --> 00:05:22.758
or whatever...
just, send me a raven, yeah?

00:05:22.758 --> 00:05:24.133
just, send me a raven, yeah?

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.091
We have Rondo

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:26.008
Oh well,

00:05:26.008 --> 00:05:27.133
you never know with him

00:05:27.466 --> 00:05:28.216
He’s a bit...

00:05:28.216 --> 00:05:29.175
(crazy whistle)

00:05:29.341 --> 00:05:31.675
You’ll definitely need a veteran backup, no?

00:05:32.091 --> 00:05:34.925
We have plenty of depth but we’ll keep you in mind

00:05:34.925 --> 00:05:35.925
Cause...you know,

00:05:35.966 --> 00:05:37.716
we could be a superteam again!

00:05:37.883 --> 00:05:39.008
Bye Rio!

00:05:39.216 --> 00:05:41.425
YOU CAN YELL AT ME ALL YOU LIKE

00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:42.466
I DON’T MIND!

00:05:44.216 --> 00:05:45.591
Alright, well...

00:05:46.925 --> 00:05:48.216
guess I’ll head to Cleveland

00:06:03.175 --> 00:06:04.216
Gadzooks!

00:06:04.883 --> 00:06:05.883
Come in, come in!  

00:06:07.508 --> 00:06:11.716
I came to say hello and welcome you to Houston

00:06:11.716 --> 00:06:13.008
Ah! Why thank you!

00:06:13.008 --> 00:06:15.175
And you must be the new scouting apprentice!

00:06:15.175 --> 00:06:16.341
I’ve been expecting you

00:06:16.716 --> 00:06:19.633
Uh...I’m your starting shooting guard...

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.050
James Harden?

00:06:22.591 --> 00:06:24.258
All Realm shooting guard?

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:28.008
James... James... you say...

00:06:28.008 --> 00:06:29.008
one moment please!

00:06:35.258 --> 00:06:36.091
Aha!

00:06:36.216 --> 00:06:37.425
James Harden!

00:06:37.425 --> 00:06:39.550
The point guard. Forgive me.

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:40.091
Shooting guard--

00:06:40.091 --> 00:06:41.800
I’ve been studying your game...

00:06:41.925 --> 00:06:44.716
it’s marvelous. Brilliant really!

00:06:45.008 --> 00:06:47.800
Oh, that’s very kind of you to say...

00:06:48.966 --> 00:06:51.716
So you...have a lot of books, I see

00:06:52.008 --> 00:06:54.841
This whole shelf is... inbound plays?

00:06:54.841 --> 00:06:55.341
Ah yes...

00:06:55.425 --> 00:06:56.716
baseline, sideline...

00:06:56.966 --> 00:06:58.966
I also keep iso plays in there somewhere

00:06:59.091 --> 00:07:00.508
for no good reason really

00:07:00.508 --> 00:07:01.841
And this shelf here,

00:07:01.841 --> 00:07:04.383
all books on the art of the pass

00:07:04.383 --> 00:07:04.925
Wow!

00:07:04.925 --> 00:07:08.133
Over there, that's tempo plays, pick and rolls...

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:09.133
you name it!

00:07:09.175 --> 00:07:11.133
Feel free to borrow them as you please, by the way

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:11.841
Wow

00:07:11.841 --> 00:07:14.550
I bet you need whole new library just for all

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.508
defensive plays

00:07:16.508 --> 00:07:17.133
Hmm?

00:07:18.633 --> 00:07:20.383
Defense...like...you know

00:07:20.425 --> 00:07:22.966
when the other team has the ball? 

00:07:23.008 --> 00:07:25.258
...And they try to...you know...score... 

00:07:25.258 --> 00:07:26.675
on... us?

00:07:26.716 --> 00:07:29.091
Oh no no no. None of that here

00:07:29.133 --> 00:07:31.133
It’s a waste of energy and it’s no fun

00:07:31.508 --> 00:07:32.341
I say

00:07:32.675 --> 00:07:33.925
half the defense...

00:07:34.591 --> 00:07:36.883
double the offense!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.083
Five minutes, Melo

00:07:49.333 --> 00:07:50.333
Understood

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:55.667
Ser Oakley

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:56.600
Carmelo...

00:07:58.417 --> 00:08:01.375
seems you’re my last friend in Knicks colors

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:02.875
Quite the opposite, actually

00:08:03.292 --> 00:08:04.458
The whole city cheers your name 

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.083
outside these Garden walls

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:08.583
I saw what they did to you

00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:10.833
More like what I did to them

00:08:11.125 --> 00:08:12.125
It’s not right

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:13.500
You’re a legend

00:08:13.875 --> 00:08:16.000
I’m just an old enforcer

00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:18.792
When I saw how the front office was treating you... 

00:08:19.042 --> 00:08:19.792
well...

00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:21.125
I did what I’ve always done...

00:08:21.542 --> 00:08:23.708
I stand up for our best players

00:08:23.708 --> 00:08:25.000
’Specially against the twonks

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.208
who run this house these days

00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:28.833
Well I’m here to return the favor

00:08:28.833 --> 00:08:30.042
Now c’mon, we don’t have much time

00:08:30.083 --> 00:08:30.583
Whaddya mean?

00:08:30.583 --> 00:08:31.417
Whaddya doin’?

00:08:31.417 --> 00:08:32.417
We’re getting you out of here

00:08:32.792 --> 00:08:34.167
Wait...who’s “we”?

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:34.917
(Whistle)

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.458
Derrick! The key!

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:37.667
Toss it now!

00:08:38.042 --> 00:08:38.542
Huh?

00:08:38.792 --> 00:08:39.667
Joakim?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.000
Where’s Derrick?

00:08:41.167 --> 00:08:41.958
He had to go

00:08:41.958 --> 00:08:43.167
He had family issues

00:08:43.167 --> 00:08:44.167
What?

00:08:44.375 --> 00:08:45.583
Well do you have the key?

00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:46.833
Uh huh, yeah...

00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:47.917
Well then toss it!

00:08:47.917 --> 00:08:50.458
Right, right. Okay, sure

00:08:57.417 --> 00:08:58.417
Oh crap

00:09:03.875 --> 00:09:04.875
Men!

00:09:05.042 --> 00:09:06.458
Do you hear that?

00:09:07.042 --> 00:09:08.625
It’s game time!

00:09:08.625 --> 00:09:10.042
YEAH!

00:09:10.083 --> 00:09:12.042
It’s early, for sure,

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.000
but if the season ended today,

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.833
we’d barely be in the eighth seed

00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:20.167
Do you want to be in the eighth seed?

00:09:20.167 --> 00:09:21.083
No!

00:09:21.083 --> 00:09:21.792
Aye!

00:09:22.583 --> 00:09:24.750
No, Thad, we don’t want that

00:09:25.208 --> 00:09:28.125
Ayyyyyye DON’T want the eighth seed

00:09:28.125 --> 00:09:29.333
I don’t want that...

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:32.833
We are the Pacers of Indiana!

00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:35.333
We don’t settle for the eighth seed

00:09:35.333 --> 00:09:35.958
No!

00:09:35.958 --> 00:09:40.042
Would Ser Reggie Miller have settled for the eighth seed?

00:09:40.042 --> 00:09:41.042
No!

00:09:41.125 --> 00:09:45.333
Would Jermaine of Neal have settled for the eighth seed?

00:09:45.333 --> 00:09:45.792
No!

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:46.375
Probably not!

00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:47.083
Would...

00:09:48.125 --> 00:09:50.958
M-Mark Jackson or...

00:09:51.333 --> 00:09:55.708
Rik Smits have settled for the eighth seed?

00:09:55.708 --> 00:09:56.958
Maybe?

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.458
Who is Rip Smith?

00:09:59.083 --> 00:10:01.708
We are not an eighth seed team!

00:10:01.708 --> 00:10:02.708
Better than that!

00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:04.875
We will not be a seventh seed team!

00:10:04.875 --> 00:10:05.875
Well, we probably will be though

00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:10.333
What I see, is MUCH better than our record

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:11.833
I see a...

00:10:11.833 --> 00:10:14.625
fifth or sixth seed team!

00:10:14.917 --> 00:10:15.917
Probably seventh

00:10:15.917 --> 00:10:19.083
Who will at BEST make it to the second round

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:20.292
FIRST!
But probably no further!

00:10:20.292 --> 00:10:21.708
But probably no further!

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:22.958
YEAH

00:10:22.958 --> 00:10:24.125
I’M OKAY WITH THAT!

00:10:24.125 --> 00:10:25.042
Right now, 

00:10:25.042 --> 00:10:28.667
our defense is 25th in the league

00:10:28.667 --> 00:10:30.792
Let's get that up to 15th!

00:10:30.792 --> 00:10:31.792
Yeah!

00:10:32.083 --> 00:10:34.375
And our offense...it’s 20th!

00:10:34.375 --> 00:10:35.042
Boo!

00:10:35.042 --> 00:10:38.292
Let's inch that up to maybe also 15!

00:10:38.292 --> 00:10:39.333
15!

00:10:39.333 --> 00:10:40.958
So let’s go out there

00:10:41.167 --> 00:10:44.333
and send those Pistons back to Detroit

00:10:44.708 --> 00:10:46.917
and fulfill our destiny!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.083
To have a decent regular season

00:10:50.625 --> 00:10:53.750
and a forgettable playoffs!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:55.125
YEAH!

00:11:11.958 --> 00:11:12.708
What is going on?

00:11:12.708 --> 00:11:14.500
Shhh....it’s the trade deadline

00:11:14.833 --> 00:11:16.541
This could be our ticket out of here

00:11:17.041 --> 00:11:18.416
Why would you want to leave?

00:11:18.625 --> 00:11:20.333
Aren’t we in line for the first pick?

00:11:20.333 --> 00:11:21.375
No, we’re not!

00:11:21.375 --> 00:11:23.708
Because that fool Billy King traded it to

00:11:23.708 --> 00:11:25.083
Boston a few years ago!

00:11:25.166 --> 00:11:25.541
What!?

00:11:25.541 --> 00:11:27.125
I know! They’re idiots--

00:11:27.125 --> 00:11:28.125
Der coming! Der coming!

00:11:28.208 --> 00:11:28.958
Back up, back up!

00:11:28.958 --> 00:11:29.875
Everybody back up!

00:11:31.541 --> 00:11:32.916
I’m sorry to announce...

00:11:33.583 --> 00:11:34.500
we have made a trade

00:11:34.583 --> 00:11:36.333
Oh yes oh yes

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.125
Please please please

00:11:40.125 --> 00:11:40.750
Bojan

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:41.458
Yeah

00:11:41.458 --> 00:11:42.458
You’re going to Washingfell

00:11:43.083 --> 00:11:43.666
Sorry

00:11:43.666 --> 00:11:44.375
Oh my god!

00:11:44.375 --> 00:11:45.208
They are like, uh...

00:11:45.208 --> 00:11:46.333
They have like...wins

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:46.791
Yes

00:11:46.791 --> 00:11:47.791
Thirty-four wins, they have

00:11:47.791 --> 00:11:48.791
THIRTY-FOUR?!

00:11:48.875 --> 00:11:51.000
Oh man, that’s like so many wins!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.541
I know you’re disappointed, but...

00:11:52.875 --> 00:11:53.583
pack your bags

00:11:54.125 --> 00:11:55.458
They expect you there on the morrow

00:11:55.458 --> 00:11:57.166
Right. Right. Oh yeah I’m very sad

00:11:57.166 --> 00:11:59.833
This is so--I’m very sad but I’ll go pack now

00:12:00.125 --> 00:12:01.250
and fight all the tears

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.333
Um...love all you guys!

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:06.458
Thanks, uh, Lord Commander--ex-Lord Commander!

00:12:06.583 --> 00:12:07.708
Oh this is so sad!

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.541
This is SO GOOD! OH I’M FREE! 

00:12:10.708 --> 00:12:13.083
I’M FREE FROM THIS PIECE OF SHIT TEAM!

00:12:13.166 --> 00:12:15.291
THIS IS THE HAPPIEST DAY OF MY LIFE!

00:12:15.583 --> 00:12:17.750
I DON’T HAVE TO BE IN STUPID BROOKLYN

00:12:17.916 --> 00:12:19.583
THIS IS THE DUMBEST PLACE

00:12:19.708 --> 00:12:21.458
WORST FRANCHISE  EVER!

00:12:21.625 --> 00:12:22.625
MAN THESE GUYS ARE F--

